{"name":"Fennel Bulb","hex":"#ddeebb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fennel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant, Foeniculum vulgare, of the parsley family, which has a sweet, anise-like flavor.","The bulb, leaves, or stalks of the plant, eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fennel"},{"term":"bulb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bulb-shaped underground portion of a plant such as a tulip, consisting of a shortened stem and many fleshy scale leaves, from which the rest of the plant may be regrown.","The medulla oblongata."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take the shape of a bulb; to swell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fennel","blocks":[{"text":"Fennel is a flowering plant species in the carrot family. It is a hardy, perennial herb with yellow flowers and feathery leaves. It is indigenous to the shores of the Mediterranean but has become widely naturalized in many parts of the world, especially on dry soils near the sea coast and on riverbanks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Foeniculum_July_2011-1a.jpg/330px-Foeniculum_July_2011-1a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fennel"},{"title":"Bulb","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a bulb is a short underground stem with fleshy leaves or leaf bases that function as food storage organs during dormancy. In gardening, plants with other kinds of storage organ are also called ornamental bulbous plants or just bulbs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Shallots-Whole.jpg/330px-Shallots-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulb"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Fenouil.jpg/250px-Fenouil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u